#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Real apps on a headless Pila, driven the way a hand does: what the
integration tests' synthetic client can't show, since real apps do things it
doesn't (GTK 4 asks to leave fullscreen as a drag on its own title bar starts).

Each app runs alone on a sealed headless Pila (a temporary
HOME, XDG directories, runtime directory and D-Bus session bus), one
1920x1080 output, with Pila's input invariants on
(PILA_HEADLESS_CHECK_INVARIANTS: a stuck grab or a lost keyboard is a panic).
Through Pila's control socket, real pointer and keyboard input:

  - a drag by the title bar (Pila's, or the app's own) moves the window as far
    as the pointer, exactly;
  - a click on the title bar, without moving, moves nothing;
  - Mod + left drag anywhere in it moves it as far as the pointer;
  - maximized, and snapped to a half, a drag by the title bar brings it back to
    its size under the pointer;
  - after each step: no grab left, the keyboard on the window, no popup.

And typing through an input method, fcitx5 with Rime's pinyin (fcitx5-foot,
fcitx5-gtk4: a terminal and a GTK 4 text field, skipped where fcitx5 or
Rime's luna_pinyin isn't installed):

  - fcitx5 becomes Pila's input method and takes the keyboard in the app;
  - "nihao" shows its candidate window next to the text cursor, on the
    screen, blurred behind as fcitx5 asks (blur on in its settings and
    theme), and a space puts the two characters into the app;
  - a binding of Pila's still runs, and (GTK) a context menu opens and closes
    with Escape while the input method holds the keyboard, leaving no grab.

And pila-launcher (launcher: built in launcher/ with cargo build --release,
or PILA_LAUNCHER_BIN; skipped where it isn't), set as `launcher`:

  - Mod+D opens it and it takes the keyboard; Mod+D hides it and shows it
    again (twice, the second run reaching the one in the background), Escape
    hides it;
  - typing finds an app, Return starts it; an app that asks for a terminal
    starts in the one given with --terminal (foot); a click on a row starts
    it; each time it hides, leaving no grab;
  - fcitx5-launcher: "nihao" shows fcitx5's candidate window by its search
    field, and a space puts the two characters into it.

And pila-bar (bar: built in launcher/ with cargo build --release, or
PILA_BAR_BIN; skipped where it isn't), started in the run:

  - a layer surface along the top edge, as wide as the output, that windows
    keep clear of (its exclusive zone) and that takes no keyboard; a
    maximized window fills the rest;
  - the pointer resting on the clock shows the date in a tooltip below the
    bar, gone when it leaves;
  - a click on a workspace goes to it and the wheel over the bar to the next
    or previous one, starting from where a binding of Pila's left it (the
    bar follows ext-workspace), and never past the last;
  - a monitor that comes gets a bar of its own, one that goes takes its bar
    along and the bar runs on; with --bottom, along the bottom edge;
  - --height 40 --output HDMI-A-1: no bar until that monitor comes, then a
    bar 40 high on it alone, back when it's plugged in again;
  - the tray (where fcitx5 and busctl are): the bar is the session's
    StatusNotifierWatcher, fcitx5's item registers, a right click opens its
    menu with a grab, a click elsewhere closes it, and the item goes when
    fcitx5 quits.

And pila-switcher (switcher: built in launcher/ with cargo build --release,
or PILA_SWITCHER_BIN; skipped where it isn't), started in the run, with
three foot windows:

  - a quick Super+Tab, there and back, shows nothing;
  - Super held with a tap of Tab shows it: an Overlay layer surface centered
    on the output, a tile per window in a row, taking no keyboard (the window switched
    to has it); another Tab keeps it; letting go of Super takes it away, on
    the window switched to;
  - a click on a tile while Alt+Tab is held switches to that window and takes
    it away, leaving no grab.

And pila-osd (osd: built in launcher/ with cargo build --release, or
PILA_OSD_BIN; skipped where it isn't), run as the volume keys run it, with a
wpctl of the run's own that says the volume, over a maximized foot:

  - `pila-osd volume` shows it: an Overlay layer surface at the bottom
    center of the output, above the bottom edge, taking no keyboard (foot
    keeps it) and no pointer (the pointer over it is on foot);
  - a second run while it's shown, muted this time, goes to the first: one
    pila-osd process, still shown; and it goes away on its own;
  - `pila-osd brightness` shows the backlight's where there's one, and
    where there's none exits with an error and shows nothing; so does
    `pila-osd volume` without wpctl.

Then it judges Pila's log (no panic, no client disconnected for a protocol
error) and prints PASS/FAIL per check; exits 1 if any failed.

  scripts/apps                       every app that's installed
  scripts/apps gtk4 foot ...         some of them (gtk4, foot, kitty,
                                     weston-terminal, xterm, launcher,
                                     bar, switcher, osd, fcitx5-foot,
                                     fcitx5-gtk4, fcitx5-launcher)

Results go to pila-apps/<app>/: Pila's log (pila.log), the app's
(app.log) and a screenshot at the end (grim, if installed). Uses
target/release/pila, or PILA_BIN. Needs python3 and dbus-run-session
(package dbus); xterm needs Xwayland; fcitx5-gtk4 reads the text back with
wl-paste (package wl-clipboard); launcher, bar, switcher and osd need foot. Standard
library only.
"""

import json
import os
import shlex
import shutil
import socket
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time

# name: (command, how it decorates itself: "pila" draws the title bar, "app"
# draws its own)
APPS = {
    "gtk4": (["gtk4-widget-factory"], "app"),
    "foot": (["foot"], "pila"),
    "kitty": (["kitty"], "pila"),
    "weston-terminal": (["weston-terminal"], "app"),
    "xterm": (["xterm"], "pila"),
}

# Typing through fcitx5: name: (the app, as a function of the file a terminal
# writes what's typed to; how the text is read back: that "file", or the
# "clipboard" after select all and copy).
IME_APPS = {
    "fcitx5-foot": (lambda typed: ["foot", "sh", "-c", f"cat > {shlex.quote(typed)}"], "file"),
    "fcitx5-gtk4": (lambda typed: ["gtk4-demo", "--run=entry_undo"], "clipboard"),
    # pila-launcher, opened with Mod+D: no command of its own.
    "fcitx5-launcher": (None, "launcher"),
}

# pila-launcher, set as `launcher` for its run.
LAUNCHER = "pila-launcher"
# pila-bar, its layer surfaces' namespace and height.
BAR_APP, BAR_HEIGHT, BAR_BUTTON = "pila-bar", 28, 28
# pila-switcher, its layer surface's namespace, and its tiles' size, the
# spacing between them and the padding around them all (`switcher/src/ui.rs`).
SWITCHER_APP, SWITCHER_TILE, SWITCHER_SPACING, SWITCHER_PADDING = "pila-switcher", (200, 157), 4, 12
# pila-osd, its layer surface's namespace, size and margin above the bottom
# edge (`osd/src/ui.rs`).
OSD_APP, OSD_SIZE, OSD_MARGIN = "pila-osd", (320, 52), 96
# Apps for it to find (in the sealed XDG_DATA_HOME): what they write to the
# runtime directory says they ran.
LAUNCHER_APPS = {
    "zephyrtest": "[Desktop Entry]\nType=Application\nName=Zephyrtest Launch\n"
                  "Exec=sh -c \"echo launched > $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/launched\"\n",
    "zephyrterm": "[Desktop Entry]\nType=Application\nName=Zephyrterm Run\nTerminal=true\n"
                  "Exec=sh -c \"echo terminal > $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/terminal\"\n",
}

# fcitx5's settings for the run: Rime as the input method, on from the start,
# with the one schema the run types in (deploying every schema takes minutes).
FCITX5_PROFILE = """[Groups/0]
Name=Default
Default Layout=us
DefaultIM=rime

[Groups/0/Items/0]
Name=keyboard-us
Layout=

[Groups/0/Items/1]
Name=rime
Layout=

[GroupOrder]
0=Default
"""
FCITX5_CONFIG = "[Behavior]\nActiveByDefault=True\n"
# Its candidate window asks for blur behind it (ext-background-effect): on in
# its settings and in its theme (the default one, with blur).
FCITX5_CLASSICUI = "Theme=blurred\nEnableBlur=True\n"
FCITX5_THEMES = "/usr/share/fcitx5/themes"
RIME_SCHEMAS = "patch:\n  schema_list:\n    - schema: luna_pinyin\n"
PINYIN, HANZI = "nihao", "\u4f60\u597d"

BAR = 28  # Pila's title bar height
DRAG = (100, 60)  # how far each drag goes
STEPS = 20


# --- Inside Pila (`--workload`) -------------------------------------------------

class Workload:
    def __init__(self, app, out):
        self.app = app
        self.out = out
        self.log = open(os.path.join(out, "steps.log"), "w", buffering=1)
        runtime = os.environ["XDG_RUNTIME_DIR"]
        self.control = os.path.join(runtime, os.environ["WAYLAND_DISPLAY"] + ".control")

    def mark(self, text):
        # Pila's log has the program's output: the judge reads these there.
        print(f"apps: {text}", flush=True)

    def check(self, label, ok, detail=""):
        self.mark(f"check {'ok' if ok else 'failed'}: {label}{'' if ok else ' (' + detail + ')'}")
        return ok

    def ctl(self, **request):
        s = socket.socket(socket.AF_UNIX)
        s.connect(self.control)
        s.sendall(json.dumps(request).encode() + b"\n")
        data = b""
        while not data.endswith(b"\n"):
            chunk = s.recv(1 << 20)
            if not chunk:
                break
            data += chunk
        s.close()
        return json.loads(data) if data.strip() else {}

    def state(self):
        return self.ctl(cmd="state")

    def window(self, state=None):
        state = state or self.state()
        windows = [w for w in state.get("windows", []) if not w.get("override_redirect")]
        return windows[0] if windows else None

    def wait(self, cond, timeout=5.0):
        end = time.monotonic() + timeout
        while True:
            state = self.state()
            try:
                if cond(state):
                    return state
            except (KeyError, TypeError, IndexError):
                pass
            if time.monotonic() > end:
                return None
            time.sleep(0.05)

    def geometry(self, state=None):
        g = self.window(state)["geometry"]
        return g["x"], g["y"], g["w"], g["h"]

    def header(self, state=None):
        """A point on the title bar: Pila's above the geometry, or the app's
        own, at its top. A quarter in, away from the title and buttons."""
        w = self.window(state)
        x, y, width, _ = self.geometry(state)
        if w.get("title_bar"):
            return x + width // 4, y - BAR // 2
        return x + width // 4, y + 12

    def move(self, x, y):
        self.ctl(cmd="move", x=x + 0.5, y=y + 0.5)

    def drag(self, start, by, button="left"):
        """Press at `start`, move by `by` in small steps, release."""
        self.move(*start)
        time.sleep(0.1)
        self.ctl(cmd="button", button=button, state="press")
        time.sleep(0.05)
        for i in range(1, STEPS + 1):
            self.move(start[0] + by[0] * i / STEPS, start[1] + by[1] * i / STEPS)
            time.sleep(0.02)
        time.sleep(0.05)
        self.ctl(cmd="button", button=button, state="release")

    def settled(self, label):
        """After a step: no grab left, the keyboard on the window, no popup."""
        state = self.wait(lambda s: not s["pointer"]["grabbed"] and s["focused"] == self.window(s)["app_id"]
                          and not s["popups"], 3)
        if state is None:
            state = self.state()
            self.check(f"{label}: no grab left, the keyboard on the window, no popup", False,
                       f"grab {state['pointer']['grab']}, focused {state['focused']}, "
                       f"{len(state['popups'])} popups")
        return state

    def tap(self, key):
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key=key, state="tap")
        time.sleep(0.15)

    def typed(self, how, path):
        """What the app has, read back as `how` says."""
        if how == "file":
            self.tap("Return")
            self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Control_L+d")
            end = time.monotonic() + 3
            while time.monotonic() < end and not (os.path.exists(path) and os.path.getsize(path)):
                time.sleep(0.1)
            return open(path).read().strip() if os.path.exists(path) else ""
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Control_L+a")
        time.sleep(0.3)
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Control_L+c")
        time.sleep(0.5)
        try:
            return subprocess.run(["wl-paste", "-n"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=5).stdout
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            return ""

    def run_ime(self):
        """Typing through fcitx5 (module docs)."""
        command, how = IME_APPS[self.app]
        self.mark(f"{self.app} begin")
        home = os.environ["HOME"]
        settings = os.path.join(home, ".config/fcitx5")
        rime = os.path.join(home, ".local/share/fcitx5/rime")
        os.makedirs(os.path.join(settings, "conf"))
        os.makedirs(rime)
        theme = os.path.join(home, ".local/share/fcitx5/themes/blurred")
        shutil.copytree(os.path.join(FCITX5_THEMES, "default"), theme)
        with open(os.path.join(theme, "theme.conf")) as f:
            text = f.read().replace("[InputPanel]\n", "[InputPanel]\nEnableBlur=True\n", 1)
        with open(os.path.join(theme, "theme.conf"), "w") as f:
            f.write(text)
        for path, text in [(os.path.join(settings, "profile"), FCITX5_PROFILE),
                           (os.path.join(settings, "config"), FCITX5_CONFIG),
                           (os.path.join(settings, "conf/classicui.conf"), FCITX5_CLASSICUI),
                           (os.path.join(rime, "default.custom.yaml"), RIME_SCHEMAS)]:
            with open(path, "w") as f:
                f.write(text)
        fcitx5 = subprocess.Popen(["fcitx5"], stdout=open(os.path.join(self.out, "fcitx5.log"), "w"),
                                  stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        try:
            self.ime_steps(command, how, rime)
        finally:
            fcitx5.terminate()
        return self.finish()

    def wait_rime(self, rime):
        """Rime compiles its dictionary the first time: it says so when done."""
        user = os.path.join(rime, "user.yaml")
        end = time.monotonic() + 120
        while time.monotonic() < end and not (os.path.exists(user) and "last_build_time" in open(user).read()):
            time.sleep(0.2)
        time.sleep(1.5)

    def ime_steps(self, command, how, rime):
        present = self.wait(lambda s: s["input_method"]["present"], 20)
        if not self.check("fcitx5 is Pila's input method", present is not None, "none within 20 s"):
            return
        if how == "launcher":
            return self.launcher_ime_steps(rime)
        typed = os.path.join(self.out, "typed.txt")
        subprocess.Popen(command(typed), stdout=open(os.path.join(self.out, "app.log"), "w"),
                         stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: self.window(s) is not None and self.window(s)["geometry"]["w"] > 0, 20)
        if not self.check(f"{command(typed)[0]} opens a window", state is not None, "none within 20 s"):
            return
        app_id = self.window(state)["app_id"]
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["keyboard_grab"] == "input_method"
                          and s["input_method"]["text_input_focus"] == app_id, 10)
        now = self.state()
        self.check("the input method takes the keyboard in the app's text field", state is not None,
                   f"keyboard grab {now['keyboard_grab']}, text input on {now['input_method']['text_input_focus']}")
        self.wait_rime(rime)

        for key in PINYIN:
            self.tap(key)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["input_method"]["popups"], 5)
        if self.check(f"typing {PINYIN!r} shows the candidate window", state is not None, "none within 5 s"):
            time.sleep(0.3)
            state = self.state()
            x, y, w, h = self.geometry(state)
            px, py, pw, ph = state["input_method"]["popups"][0]["geometry"]
            screen = state["outputs"][0]["geometry"]
            # Below the first line of a terminal, or below a text field in
            # the window: never over the window's top-left corner, where it
            # goes with no text cursor known.
            at_text = x <= px < x + w and y < py <= y + h + ph
            on_screen = (0 <= px and px + pw <= screen["w"] and 0 <= py and py + ph <= screen["h"])
            self.check("the candidate window is next to the text cursor, on the screen",
                       at_text and on_screen, f"it's at {(px, py, pw, ph)}, the window at {(x, y, w, h)}")
            blurred = self.wait(lambda s: s["blur"]["entries"] > 0, 3)
            self.check("the candidate window is blurred behind, as fcitx5 asks", blurred is not None,
                       "no backdrop within 3 s")
            if shutil.which("grim"):
                subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "candidates.png")], check=False)
        self.tap("space")
        gone = self.wait(lambda s: not s["input_method"]["popups"], 5)
        self.check("a space closes the candidate window", gone is not None)

        # A binding of Pila's, with the input method holding the keyboard.
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+m")
        maximized = self.wait(lambda s: self.window(s)["maximized"], 3)
        self.check("Super+m maximizes the window while the input method holds the keyboard",
                   maximized is not None)
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+m")
        self.wait(lambda s: not self.window(s)["maximized"], 3)
        time.sleep(0.5)

        if how == "clipboard":
            # A context menu in the text field: it opens, Escape closes it,
            # and typing goes on.
            x, y, w, _ = self.geometry()
            self.move(x + w // 2, y + 100)
            time.sleep(0.3)
            self.ctl(cmd="button", button="right", state="click")
            opened = self.wait(lambda s: s["popups"], 3)
            self.check("a context menu opens while the input method holds the keyboard", opened is not None)
            time.sleep(0.3)
            self.tap("Escape")
            closed = self.wait(lambda s: not s["popups"] and not s["pointer"]["grabbed"], 3)
            now = self.state()
            self.check("Escape closes it and no grab is left", closed is not None,
                       f"{len(now['popups'])} popups, pointer grab {now['pointer']['grab']}")
            for key in PINYIN:
                self.tap(key)
            self.tap("space")
            time.sleep(0.3)
            expected = HANZI * 2
        else:
            expected = HANZI
        got = self.typed(how, typed)
        self.check(f"{PINYIN!r} and a space put {expected!r} into the app", got == expected, f"it has {got!r}")

    # --- pila-bar ---

    def bars(self, state):
        return [l for l in state["layers"] if l["namespace"] == BAR_APP]

    def start_bar(self, *args):
        return subprocess.Popen([os.environ["PILA_APPS_BAR"], *args],
                                stdout=open(os.path.join(self.out, "bar.log"), "a"), stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)

    def stop_bar(self, bar, label):
        bar.terminate()
        bar.wait(5)
        gone = self.wait(lambda s: not self.bars(s) and s["outputs"][0]["usable"]["h"] == 1080, 5)
        return self.check(label, gone is not None, f"layers {self.bars(self.state())}")

    def wheel(self, notches):
        self.ctl(cmd="axis", v=notches)
        time.sleep(0.2)

    def run_bar(self):
        """pila-bar (module docs)."""
        self.mark(f"{self.app} begin")
        bar = self.start_bar()
        # Its first frame: the surface mapped at its size.
        state = self.wait(lambda s: any(l["geometry"] and l["geometry"]["h"] for l in self.bars(s)), 20)
        if not self.check("pila-bar opens a layer surface", state is not None, "none within 20 s"):
            bar.terminate()
            return self.finish()
        layer, = self.bars(state)
        g, usable = layer["geometry"], state["outputs"][0]["usable"]
        self.check("along the top edge, as wide as the output, on the Top layer",
                   (g["x"], g["y"], g["w"], g["h"]) == (0, 0, 1920, BAR_HEIGHT) and layer["layer"] == "top",
                   f"{layer['layer']} at {g}")
        self.check("windows keep clear of it, and it takes no keyboard",
                   layer["exclusive_zone"] == BAR_HEIGHT and (usable["y"], usable["h"]) == (BAR_HEIGHT, 1080 - BAR_HEIGHT)
                   and layer["keyboard"] == "none", f"zone {layer['exclusive_zone']}, usable {usable}, "
                   f"keyboard {layer['keyboard']}")

        subprocess.Popen(["foot"], stdout=open(os.path.join(self.out, "app.log"), "w"), stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: self.window(s) is not None and self.window(s)["geometry"]["w"] > 0
                          and s["focused"] == self.window(s)["app_id"], 20)
        if not self.check("foot opens a window, focused", state is not None, "none within 20 s"):
            bar.terminate()
            return self.finish()
        time.sleep(1)
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+m")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: self.window(s)["maximized"], 3)
        if self.check("Super+m maximizes it", state is not None):
            time.sleep(0.5)
            state = self.state()
            x, y, w, h = self.geometry(state)
            top = y - (BAR if self.window(state).get("title_bar") else 0)
            self.check("a maximized window fills the output below the bar",
                       (x, top, w, y + h) == (0, BAR_HEIGHT, 1920, 1080), f"geometry {(x, y, w, h)}")
        if shutil.which("grim"):
            subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "bar.png")], check=False)

        # The clock's tooltip (the date): a layer surface of its own below the
        # bar while the pointer rests on the clock (the last block: the time
        # alone), taking no input; gone when the pointer leaves.
        tooltip = lambda s: next((l for l in s["layers"] if l["namespace"] == "pila-bar-tooltip"
                                  and l["geometry"] and l["geometry"]["h"]), None)
        self.move(1920 - 30, BAR_HEIGHT // 2)
        state = self.wait(tooltip, 5)
        if self.check("the pointer resting on the clock shows its tooltip", state is not None,
                      f"layers {[l['namespace'] for l in self.state()['layers']]}"):
            g = tooltip(state)["geometry"]
            self.check("below the bar, inside the output, with no grab or keyboard",
                       g["y"] >= BAR_HEIGHT and g["x"] >= 0 and g["x"] + g["w"] <= 1920
                       and not state["pointer"]["grabbed"] and tooltip(state)["keyboard"] == "none",
                       f"at {g}, grabbed {state['pointer']['grabbed']}")
            if shutil.which("grim"):
                time.sleep(0.5)  # Past its opening animation, for the picture.
                subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "tooltip.png")], check=False)
        self.move(960, 600)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: tooltip(s) is None, 5)
        self.check("and leaving the clock hides it", state is not None)

        # A click on the second workspace's button.
        self.move(BAR_BUTTON + BAR_BUTTON // 2, BAR_HEIGHT // 2)
        time.sleep(0.2)
        self.ctl(cmd="button", button="left", state="click")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["workspace"] == 2 and not s["pointer"]["grabbed"], 3)
        self.check("a click on a workspace goes to it, leaving no grab", state is not None,
                   f"on workspace {self.state()['workspace']}")
        # Back by a binding of Pila's: the wheel goes on from there.
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+Page_Up")
        self.wait(lambda s: s["workspace"] == 1, 3)
        time.sleep(0.5)
        self.move(960, BAR_HEIGHT // 2)
        self.wheel(1)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["workspace"] == 2, 3)
        self.check("the wheel down goes to the next workspace, from where a binding left it",
                   state is not None, f"on workspace {self.state()['workspace']}")
        for _ in range(5):
            self.wheel(1)
            time.sleep(0.3)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["workspace"] == 4, 3)
        time.sleep(0.5)
        self.check("and never past the last", self.state()["workspace"] == 4,
                   f"on workspace {self.state()['workspace']}")
        self.wheel(-1)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["workspace"] == 3, 3)
        self.check("the wheel up goes to the previous one", state is not None,
                   f"on workspace {self.state()['workspace']}")
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+1")
        self.wait(lambda s: s["workspace"] == 1, 3)
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+m")
        self.wait(lambda s: not self.window(s)["maximized"], 3)

        # Monitors that come and go.
        self.ctl(cmd="output_add", spec="HDMI-A-1:1280x720@60")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: sorted(l["output"] for l in self.bars(s) if l["geometry"]
                                           and l["geometry"]["h"]) == ["HDMI-A-1", "eDP-1"], 10)
        self.check("a monitor that comes gets a bar of its own", state is not None,
                   f"layers {self.bars(self.state())}")
        if state is not None:
            layer = next(l for l in self.bars(state) if l["output"] == "HDMI-A-1")
            self.check("as wide as that monitor", layer["geometry"]["w"] == 1280, f"at {layer['geometry']}")
        self.ctl(cmd="output_remove", name="HDMI-A-1")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: [l["output"] for l in self.bars(s)] == ["eDP-1"], 5)
        time.sleep(0.5)
        self.check("one that goes takes its bar along, and the bar runs on",
                   state is not None and bar.poll() is None, f"exit status {bar.poll()}")
        self.stop_bar(bar, "the bar gone, windows have the whole output again")

        bar = self.start_bar("--bottom")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: any(l["geometry"] and l["geometry"]["h"] for l in self.bars(s)), 20)
        if self.check("pila-bar --bottom opens a layer surface", state is not None, "none within 20 s"):
            g, usable = self.bars(state)[0]["geometry"], state["outputs"][0]["usable"]
            self.check("along the bottom edge, which windows keep clear of",
                       (g["y"], g["h"]) == (1080 - BAR_HEIGHT, BAR_HEIGHT)
                       and (usable["y"], usable["h"]) == (0, 1080 - BAR_HEIGHT), f"at {g}, usable {usable}")
        self.stop_bar(bar, "gone again")

        # Only on the monitor named, as high as asked, also once it comes back.
        bar = self.start_bar("--height", "40", "--output", "HDMI-A-1")
        time.sleep(2)
        self.check("pila-bar --output HDMI-A-1 opens nothing while there's no HDMI-A-1",
                   not self.bars(self.state()) and bar.poll() is None,
                   f"layers {self.bars(self.state())}, exit status {bar.poll()}")
        self.ctl(cmd="output_add", spec="HDMI-A-1:1280x720@60")
        shown = lambda s: [(l["output"], l["geometry"] and l["geometry"]["h"]) for l in self.bars(s)] \
            == [("HDMI-A-1", 40)]
        state = self.wait(shown, 10)
        self.check("then a bar on HDMI-A-1 alone, 40 high", state is not None, f"layers {self.bars(self.state())}")
        if state is not None:
            layer = next(l for l in self.bars(state))
            self.check("whose exclusive zone is its height", layer["exclusive_zone"] == 40,
                       f"zone {layer['exclusive_zone']}")
        self.ctl(cmd="output_remove", name="HDMI-A-1")
        self.wait(lambda s: not self.bars(s), 5)
        self.ctl(cmd="output_add", spec="HDMI-A-1:1280x720@60")
        state = self.wait(shown, 10)
        self.check("unplugged and plugged again, it's back", state is not None,
                   f"layers {self.bars(self.state())}")
        self.ctl(cmd="output_remove", name="HDMI-A-1")
        self.stop_bar(bar, "and gone with it")
        self.bar_tray()
        return self.finish()

    def bar_tray(self):
        """The tray: the bar is the session's StatusNotifierWatcher, a real
        item (fcitx5's) registers with it, shows its tooltip while the pointer
        rests on it, its menu opens on a right click
        with a grab that a click elsewhere ends, and the item goes when
        fcitx5 quits. With no battery or clock, the item is the last block."""
        if not (shutil.which("fcitx5") and shutil.which("busctl")):
            return
        def busctl(*args):
            out = subprocess.run(["busctl", "--user", *args], capture_output=True, text=True)
            return out.stdout.strip()
        bar = self.start_bar("--no-battery", "--clock", "")
        self.wait(lambda s: any(l["geometry"] and l["geometry"]["h"] for l in self.bars(s)), 20)
        watcher = ("org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher", "/StatusNotifierWatcher", "org.kde.StatusNotifierWatcher")
        end = time.monotonic() + 10
        owner = ""
        while owner != f"u {bar.pid}" and time.monotonic() < end:
            owner = busctl("call", "org.freedesktop.DBus", "/org/freedesktop/DBus", "org.freedesktop.DBus",
                           "GetConnectionUnixProcessID", "s", watcher[0])
            time.sleep(0.2)
        self.check("pila-bar is the tray's StatusNotifierWatcher", owner == f"u {bar.pid}", owner or "no owner")
        fcitx = subprocess.Popen(["fcitx5"], stdout=open(os.path.join(self.out, "fcitx5.log"), "w"),
                                 stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        registered = lambda: busctl("get-property", *watcher, "RegisteredStatusNotifierItems")
        end = time.monotonic() + 15
        while registered() in ("", "as 0") and time.monotonic() < end:
            time.sleep(0.2)
        self.check("fcitx5's tray item registers with it", registered() not in ("", "as 0"), registered())
        # Resting on its icon shows its tooltip (its ToolTip, or its title),
        # below the bar, under the pointer and inside the output.
        time.sleep(1.5)
        tooltip = lambda s: next((l for l in s["layers"] if l["namespace"] == "pila-bar-tooltip"
                                  and l["geometry"] and l["geometry"]["h"]), None)
        icon_x = 1920 - BAR_HEIGHT // 2
        self.move(icon_x, BAR_HEIGHT // 2)
        state = self.wait(tooltip, 5)
        if self.check("resting on its icon shows its tooltip", state is not None,
                      f"layers {[l['namespace'] for l in self.state()['layers']]}"):
            g = tooltip(state)["geometry"]
            self.check("below the bar, under the pointer, inside the output",
                       g["y"] >= BAR_HEIGHT and g["x"] <= icon_x <= g["x"] + g["w"]
                       and g["x"] >= 0 and g["x"] + g["w"] <= 1920 and not state["pointer"]["grabbed"],
                       f"at {g}")
            if shutil.which("grim"):
                time.sleep(0.5)
                subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "tray-tooltip.png")], check=False)
        self.move(960, 600)
        self.check("and gone when the pointer leaves it", self.wait(lambda s: tooltip(s) is None, 5) is not None)
        # Its menu is read ahead by now: a right click.
        self.move(icon_x, BAR_HEIGHT // 2)
        time.sleep(0.2)
        self.ctl(cmd="button", button="right", state="click")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["popups"] and s["pointer"]["grabbed"], 5)
        self.check("a right click on its icon opens its menu, with a grab", state is not None,
                   f"popups {self.state()['popups']}, grabbed {self.state()['pointer']['grabbed']}")
        if shutil.which("grim"):
            time.sleep(0.5)
            subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "tray.png")], check=False)
        self.move(960, 600)
        time.sleep(0.2)
        self.ctl(cmd="button", button="left", state="click")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: not s["popups"] and not s["pointer"]["grabbed"], 5)
        self.check("a click elsewhere closes it, leaving no grab", state is not None,
                   f"popups {self.state()['popups']}")
        fcitx.terminate()
        fcitx.wait(5)
        end = time.monotonic() + 10
        while registered() != "as 0" and time.monotonic() < end:
            time.sleep(0.2)
        self.check("the item leaves when fcitx5 quits, the bar running on",
                   registered() == "as 0" and bar.poll() is None, f"{registered()}, exit status {bar.poll()}")
        self.stop_bar(bar, "the tray's bar gone")

    # --- pila-launcher ---

    def launcher_layer(self, state):
        return next((l for l in state["layers"] if l["namespace"] == LAUNCHER), None)

    def launcher_shown(self, state):
        return self.launcher_layer(state) is not None and state["keyboard_focus"] == "layer:" + LAUNCHER

    def open_launcher(self, label):
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+d")
        state = self.wait(self.launcher_shown, 20)
        self.check(label, state is not None, "not within 20 s")
        time.sleep(0.3)
        return state

    def launcher_hidden(self, label, timeout=5):
        state = self.wait(lambda s: self.launcher_layer(s) is None and not s["pointer"]["grabbed"], timeout)
        return self.check(label, state is not None, "still shown")

    def ran(self, name, timeout=10):
        """Whether an app of LAUNCHER_APPS wrote its file."""
        path = os.path.join(os.environ["XDG_RUNTIME_DIR"], name)
        end = time.monotonic() + timeout
        while time.monotonic() < end:
            if os.path.exists(path) and os.path.getsize(path):
                os.remove(path)
                return True
            time.sleep(0.1)
        return False

    def launcher_ime_steps(self, rime):
        """Typing into pila-launcher's search field through fcitx5 (module docs)."""
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+d")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: self.launcher_shown(s) and s["keyboard_grab"] == "input_method"
                          and s["input_method"]["text_input_focus"] == LAUNCHER, 20)
        now = self.state()
        if not self.check("the input method takes the keyboard in the launcher's search field",
                          state is not None,
                          f"keyboard on {now['keyboard_focus']}, grab {now['keyboard_grab']}, "
                          f"text input on {now['input_method']['text_input_focus']}"):
            return
        self.wait_rime(rime)
        for key in PINYIN:
            self.tap(key)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["input_method"]["popups"], 5)
        if self.check(f"typing {PINYIN!r} shows the candidate window", state is not None, "none within 5 s"):
            time.sleep(0.3)
            state = self.state()
            popup = state["input_method"]["popups"][0]
            px, py, pw, ph = popup["geometry"]
            g = self.launcher_layer(state)["geometry"]
            screen = state["outputs"][0]["geometry"]
            by_field = g["x"] <= px < g["x"] + g["w"] and g["y"] < py < g["y"] + g["h"]
            on_screen = 0 <= px and px + pw <= screen["w"] and 0 <= py and py + ph <= screen["h"]
            self.check("the candidate window is the launcher's, by its search field, on the screen",
                       popup["parent"] == LAUNCHER and by_field and on_screen,
                       f"{popup['parent']}'s at {(px, py, pw, ph)}, the launcher at {g}")
            if shutil.which("grim"):
                subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "candidates.png")], check=False)
        self.tap("space")
        gone = self.wait(lambda s: not s["input_method"]["popups"], 5)
        self.check("a space closes the candidate window", gone is not None)
        time.sleep(0.5)
        if shutil.which("grim"):
            subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "typed.png")], check=False)
        got = self.typed("clipboard", None)
        self.check(f"{PINYIN!r} and a space put {HANZI!r} into the search field", got == HANZI,
                   f"it has {got!r}")
        self.tap("Escape")
        self.launcher_hidden("Escape hides the launcher, leaving no grab")

    def run_launcher(self):
        """pila-launcher (module docs)."""
        self.mark(f"{self.app} begin")
        apps = os.path.join(os.environ["XDG_DATA_HOME"], "applications")
        os.makedirs(apps, exist_ok=True)
        for name, entry in LAUNCHER_APPS.items():
            with open(os.path.join(apps, f"{name}.desktop"), "w") as f:
                f.write(entry)
        if not self.open_launcher("Mod+D opens pila-launcher, which takes the keyboard"):
            return self.finish()
        if shutil.which("grim"):
            subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "launcher.png")], check=False)
        # Each run after the first hands the request to the one in the
        # background, which shows a new layer surface each time.
        for which in ("once", "twice"):
            self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+d")
            self.launcher_hidden(f"Mod+D hides it ({which})")
            self.open_launcher(f"Mod+D shows it again ({which})")
        running = launcher_processes()
        self.check("one pila-launcher runs, in the background", len(running) == 1, f"pids {running}")
        self.tap("Escape")
        self.launcher_hidden("Escape hides it")

        self.open_launcher("it opens again")
        for key in "zephyrtest":
            self.tap(key)
        time.sleep(0.5)
        self.tap("Return")
        self.check("typing finds an app and Return starts it", self.ran("launched"))
        self.launcher_hidden("starting an app hides it")

        self.open_launcher("it opens for an app that asks for a terminal")
        for key in "zephyrterm":
            self.tap(key)
        time.sleep(0.5)
        self.tap("Return")
        self.check("an app with Terminal=true starts in the --terminal one", self.ran("terminal", 20))
        self.launcher_hidden("it hides then too")

        self.open_launcher("it opens for a click")
        for key in "zephyrtest":
            self.tap(key)
        time.sleep(0.5)
        g = self.launcher_layer(self.state())["geometry"]
        # The first row, below the search field.
        self.move(g["x"] + g["w"] // 2, g["y"] + 80)
        time.sleep(0.2)
        self.ctl(cmd="button", button="left", state="click")
        self.check("a click on an app starts it", self.ran("launched"))
        self.launcher_hidden("and hides it, leaving no grab")
        return self.finish()

    # --- pila-switcher ---

    def switchers(self, state):
        return [l for l in state["layers"] if l["namespace"] == SWITCHER_APP]

    def switcher_shown(self, state):
        return any(l["geometry"] and l["geometry"]["h"] for l in self.switchers(state))

    def run_switcher(self):
        """pila-switcher (module docs)."""
        self.mark(f"{self.app} begin")
        switcher = subprocess.Popen([os.environ["PILA_APPS_SWITCHER"]],
                                    stdout=open(os.path.join(self.out, "switcher.log"), "a"),
                                    stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        names = ["switch-a", "switch-b", "switch-c"]
        for name in names:
            subprocess.Popen(["foot", "--app-id", name, "--title", f"{name} window"],
                             stdout=open(os.path.join(self.out, "app.log"), "a"), stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
            if not self.check(f"{name} opens", self.wait(lambda s: s["focused"] == name, 20) is not None):
                switcher.terminate()
                return self.finish()
        # Its connection to Pila: a switch before it's subscribed would go unseen.
        time.sleep(1.5)

        # A quick Super+Tab: back and forth, nothing shown.
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Super_L", state="press")
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Tab", state="tap")
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Super_L", state="release")
        flashed = self.wait(self.switcher_shown, 0.6)
        self.check("a quick Super+Tab shows nothing", flashed is None, "a pila-switcher surface came")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["focused"] == "switch-b", 3) or self.state()
        # Most recent first: the switch goes to the second, then the third.
        second, third = state["focus_history"][1:3]

        # Held: shown after its delay, centered, a row per window, no keyboard.
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Super_L", state="press")
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Tab", state="tap")
        state = self.wait(self.switcher_shown, 5)
        if not self.check("Super held with a tap of Tab shows pila-switcher", state is not None,
                          "no surface within 5 s"):
            self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Super_L", state="release")
            switcher.terminate()
            return self.finish()
        layer, = self.switchers(state)
        g = layer["geometry"]
        width = 2 * SWITCHER_PADDING + len(names) * SWITCHER_TILE[0] + (len(names) - 1) * SWITCHER_SPACING
        height = 2 * SWITCHER_PADDING + SWITCHER_TILE[1]
        self.check("an Overlay centered on the output, a tile per window in a row",
                   layer["layer"] == "overlay" and (g["w"], g["h"]) == (width, height)
                   and abs(g["x"] + g["w"] / 2 - 960) <= 1 and abs(g["y"] + g["h"] / 2 - 540) <= 1,
                   f"{layer['layer']} at {g}")
        self.check("it takes no keyboard: the window switched to has it",
                   layer["keyboard"] == "none" and state["focused"] == second
                   and state["keyboard_focus"] != "layer:" + SWITCHER_APP,
                   f"keyboard {layer['keyboard']}, focused {state['focused']}, "
                   f"keyboard focus {state['keyboard_focus']}")
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Tab", state="tap")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["focused"] == third, 3)
        self.check("another Tab steps on, still shown", state is not None and self.switcher_shown(state))
        if shutil.which("grim"):
            time.sleep(0.3)
            subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "switcher.png")], check=False)
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Super_L", state="release")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: not self.switchers(s), 3)
        self.check("letting go of Super takes it away, on the window switched to",
                   state is not None and state["focused"] == third,
                   f"layers {self.switchers(self.state())}, focused {self.state()['focused']}")

        # A click on a row, Alt+Tab held (Alt isn't Mod here; with Mod, the same).
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Alt_L", state="press")
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Tab", state="tap")
        state = self.wait(self.switcher_shown, 5)
        if self.check("Alt+Tab held shows it too", state is not None):
            g = self.switchers(state)[0]["geometry"]
            # The last tile: the least recent window.
            tile = len(names) - 1
            self.move(g["x"] + SWITCHER_PADDING + tile * (SWITCHER_TILE[0] + SWITCHER_SPACING) + SWITCHER_TILE[0] // 2,
                      g["y"] + SWITCHER_PADDING + SWITCHER_TILE[1] // 2)
            time.sleep(0.2)
            last = state["focus_history"][-1]
            self.ctl(cmd="button", button="left", state="click")
            state = self.wait(lambda s: not self.switchers(s) and s["focused"] == last, 3)
            now = self.state()
            self.check("a click on a tile switches to that window and takes it away, no grab left",
                       state is not None and not now["pointer"]["grabbed"],
                       f"focused {now['focused']} (wanted {last}), layers {self.switchers(now)}, "
                       f"grab {now['pointer']['grab']}")
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Alt_L", state="release")
        switcher.terminate()
        switcher.wait(5)
        return self.finish()

    # --- pila-osd ---

    def osds(self, state):
        return [l for l in state["layers"] if l["namespace"] == OSD_APP and l["geometry"]
                and l["geometry"]["h"]]

    def osd_processes(self):
        mine = f"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR={os.environ['XDG_RUNTIME_DIR']}".encode()
        count = 0
        for pid in filter(str.isdigit, os.listdir("/proc")):
            try:
                with open(f"/proc/{pid}/stat") as f:
                    stat = f.read()
                with open(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline", "rb") as f:
                    argv0 = f.read().split(b"\0")[0].decode(errors="replace")
                with open(f"/proc/{pid}/environ", "rb") as f:
                    environ = f.read().split(b"\0")
            except OSError:
                continue
            if os.path.basename(argv0) == OSD_APP and mine in environ and stat.rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[0] != "Z":
                count += 1
        return count

    def run_osd(self):
        """pila-osd (module docs)."""
        self.mark(f"{self.app} begin")
        osd = os.environ["PILA_APPS_OSD"]
        # A wpctl of the run's own: the volume it says is in a file.
        bin_dir = os.path.join(os.environ["XDG_RUNTIME_DIR"], "osd-bin")
        os.makedirs(bin_dir, exist_ok=True)
        said = os.path.join(bin_dir, "volume")
        with open(os.path.join(bin_dir, "wpctl"), "w") as f:
            f.write(f"#!/bin/sh\ncat {shlex.quote(said)}\n")
        os.chmod(os.path.join(bin_dir, "wpctl"), 0o755)
        env = dict(os.environ, PATH=bin_dir + ":" + os.environ["PATH"])
        log = open(os.path.join(self.out, "osd.log"), "a")

        def run(*args, path=None):
            return subprocess.Popen([osd, *args], stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,
                                    env=dict(env, PATH=path) if path else env)

        subprocess.Popen(["foot"], stdout=open(os.path.join(self.out, "app.log"), "w"), stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        if not self.check("foot opens", self.wait(lambda s: s["focused"] == "foot", 20) is not None):
            return self.finish()
        self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys="Super+m")
        self.wait(lambda s: self.window(s)["maximized"], 3)

        with open(said, "w") as f:
            f.write("Volume: 0.45\n")
        first = run("volume")
        state = self.wait(lambda s: self.osds(s), 20)
        if not self.check("pila-osd volume shows it", state is not None, "no surface within 20 s"):
            first.terminate()
            return self.finish()
        layer, = self.osds(state)
        g, (w, h) = layer["geometry"], OSD_SIZE
        self.check("an Overlay at the bottom center, above the bottom edge",
                   layer["layer"] == "overlay" and (g["w"], g["h"]) == (w, h)
                   and g["x"] == (1920 - w) // 2 and g["y"] == 1080 - OSD_MARGIN - h, f"{layer['layer']} at {g}")
        self.move(g["x"] + w // 2, g["y"] + h // 2)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: s["pointer"]["focus"] == "foot", 2) or self.state()
        self.check("it takes no keyboard and no pointer: foot keeps both",
                   layer["keyboard"] == "none" and state["focused"] == "foot"
                   and state["pointer"]["focus"] == "foot",
                   f"keyboard {layer['keyboard']}, focused {state['focused']}, pointer on {state['pointer']['focus']}")
        if shutil.which("grim"):
            subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "osd.png")], check=False)

        with open(said, "w") as f:
            f.write("Volume: 0.40 [MUTED]\n")
        second = run("volume")
        second.wait(5)
        state = self.state()
        self.check("a second run goes to the first: one pila-osd, still shown",
                   second.returncode == 0 and self.osd_processes() == 1 and self.osds(state),
                   f"exit {second.returncode}, {self.osd_processes()} processes, layers {self.osds(state)}")
        if shutil.which("grim"):
            time.sleep(0.2)
            subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "osd-muted.png")], check=False)
        gone = self.wait(lambda s: not self.osds(s), 4)
        self.check("it goes away on its own", gone is not None)

        brightness = run("brightness")
        brightness.wait(5)
        if os.listdir("/sys/class/backlight") if os.path.isdir("/sys/class/backlight") else []:
            shown = self.wait(lambda s: self.osds(s), 3)
            self.check("pila-osd brightness shows the backlight's", brightness.returncode == 0 and shown is not None,
                       f"exit {brightness.returncode}")
            self.wait(lambda s: not self.osds(s), 4)
        else:
            self.check("pila-osd brightness without a backlight exits with an error",
                       brightness.returncode == 1 and not self.osds(self.state()), f"exit {brightness.returncode}")
        no_wpctl = run("volume", path="/nonexistent")
        no_wpctl.wait(5)
        self.check("pila-osd volume without wpctl exits with an error and shows nothing",
                   no_wpctl.returncode == 1 and not self.osds(self.state()), f"exit {no_wpctl.returncode}")
        first.terminate()
        first.wait(5)
        return self.finish()

    def run(self):
        if self.app == "osd":
            return self.run_osd()
        if self.app == "switcher":
            return self.run_switcher()
        if self.app in IME_APPS:
            return self.run_ime()
        if self.app == "launcher":
            return self.run_launcher()
        if self.app == "bar":
            return self.run_bar()
        command, _ = APPS[self.app]
        self.mark(f"{self.app} begin")
        appdir = os.path.join(self.out, "app.log")
        subprocess.Popen(command, stdout=open(appdir, "w"), stderr=subprocess.STDOUT)
        state = self.wait(lambda s: self.window(s) is not None and self.window(s)["geometry"]["w"] > 0, 20)
        if not self.check(f"{self.app} opens a window", state is not None, "none within 20 s"):
            return self.finish()
        # Let it settle (fonts, a second configure).
        time.sleep(1.5)
        state = self.state()
        w = self.window(state)
        self.mark(f"window {w['app_id']}, {'Pila' if w.get('title_bar') else 'its own'} title bar, "
                  f"geometry {self.geometry(state)}")
        self.wait(lambda s: s["focused"] == self.window(s)["app_id"], 3)

        # A drag by the title bar.
        before = self.geometry()
        self.drag(self.header(), DRAG)
        state = self.settled("drag by the title bar")
        after = self.geometry(state)
        moved = (after[0] - before[0], after[1] - before[1])
        self.check("a drag by the title bar moves it as far as the pointer",
                   moved == DRAG and after[2:] == before[2:],
                   f"moved {moved}, size {before[2:]} -> {after[2:]}")

        # A click on it, without moving.
        before = self.geometry()
        self.move(*self.header())
        time.sleep(0.1)
        self.ctl(cmd="button", button="left", state="click")
        time.sleep(0.5)
        state = self.settled("click on the title bar")
        self.check("a click on the title bar moves nothing", self.geometry(state) == before,
                   f"{before} -> {self.geometry(state)}")

        # Mod + left drag from the middle.
        before = self.geometry()
        middle = (before[0] + before[2] // 2, before[1] + before[3] // 2)
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Super_L", state="press")
        self.drag(middle, (-DRAG[0], -DRAG[1]))
        self.ctl(cmd="key", key="Super_L", state="release")
        state = self.settled("Mod+drag")
        after = self.geometry(state)
        moved = (after[0] - before[0], after[1] - before[1])
        self.check("Mod + left drag moves it as far as the pointer", moved == (-DRAG[0], -DRAG[1]),
                   f"moved {moved}")

        # Maximized and snapped, then dragged by the title bar.
        size = self.geometry()[2:]
        for combo, what in [("Super+m", "maximized"), ("Super+Left", "snapped")]:
            self.ctl(cmd="combo", keys=combo)
            filled = self.wait(lambda s: self.geometry(s)[2:] != size
                               and (self.window(s)["maximized"] or self.window(s)["snapped"]), 3)
            if not self.check(f"{combo} gets it {what}", filled is not None):
                continue
            time.sleep(0.5)
            start = self.header()
            # How far down the press is from the top of the geometry.
            pressed_at = start[1] - self.geometry()[1]
            self.drag(start, (40, 120))
            back = self.wait(lambda s: self.geometry(s)[2:] == size, 3)
            self.settled(f"drag out of {what}")
            state = back or self.state()
            x, y, width, _ = self.geometry(state)
            px, py = start[0] + 40, start[1] + 120
            top = y - BAR if self.window(state).get("title_bar") else y
            # A snapped window keeps the pointer where it was pressed on its
            # title bar; a maximized one is put under it at a set height.
            keeps = abs((py - y) - pressed_at) <= 2 if what == "snapped" else top <= py < y + 40
            self.check(f"{what}, a drag by the title bar brings it back to its size under the pointer",
                       back is not None and x <= px < x + width and keeps
                       and not self.window(state)["maximized"] and not self.window(state)["snapped"],
                       f"size {self.geometry(state)[2:]} (was {size}), pointer ({px}, {py}) "
                       f"vs {self.geometry(state)}, pressed {pressed_at} px from its top, "
                       f"now {py - y}")
        return self.finish()

    def finish(self):
        if shutil.which("grim"):
            subprocess.run(["grim", os.path.join(self.out, "end.png")], check=False)
        self.mark(f"{self.app} done")
        time.sleep(0.3)
        self.ctl(cmd="quit")


# --- Outside: a sealed headless Pila per app, and the judge ----------------------

def launcher_processes():
    """The pids of this run's pila-launcher processes still running (by
    their sealed runtime directory)."""
    mine = f"XDG_RUNTIME_DIR={os.environ['XDG_RUNTIME_DIR']}".encode()
    pids = []
    for pid in filter(str.isdigit, os.listdir("/proc")):
        try:
            with open(f"/proc/{pid}/stat") as f:
                stat = f.read()
            with open(f"/proc/{pid}/cmdline", "rb") as f:
                argv0 = f.read().split(b"\0")[0].decode(errors="replace")
            with open(f"/proc/{pid}/environ", "rb") as f:
                environ = f.read().split(b"\0")
        except OSError:
            continue
        # Zombies don't count: a run that handed its request over and exited.
        if os.path.basename(argv0) == LAUNCHER and mine in environ and stat.rsplit(")", 1)[1].split()[0] != "Z":
            pids.append(int(pid))
    return pids


def judge(app, out):
    log = open(os.path.join(out, "pila.log"), errors="replace").read()
    results = []

    def result(ok, label):
        results.append(ok)
        print(f"{'PASS' if ok else 'FAIL'}  {label}")

    if f"apps: {app} done" not in log:
        result(False, f"the steps finished (Pila quit or crashed before; see {out}/pila.log)")
    result("panicked" not in log and "pila crashed" not in log,
           "Pila didn't panic (input invariants included)")
    errors = [line for line in log.splitlines() if "client disconnected by a protocol error" in line]
    result(not errors, "no client was disconnected for a protocol error")
    for line in errors[:3]:
        print(f"      {line.strip()[:160]}")
    for line in log.splitlines():
        if "apps: window " in line:
            print(f"      {line.split('apps: ', 1)[1]}")
        elif "apps: check ok: " in line:
            result(True, line.split("apps: check ok: ", 1)[1])
        elif "apps: check failed: " in line:
            result(False, line.split("apps: check failed: ", 1)[1])
    return all(results)


def data_file(relative):
    """Whether a data directory of the system has `relative`."""
    dirs = os.environ.get("XDG_DATA_DIRS") or "/usr/local/share:/usr/share"
    return any(os.path.exists(os.path.join(d, relative)) for d in dirs.split(":") if d)


def missing_for(app, launcher, bar, switcher, osd):
    """What `app`'s run needs and the system lacks, if anything (`launcher`,
    `bar`, `switcher`, `osd`: pila-launcher's, pila-bar's, pila-switcher's and
    pila-osd's binaries)."""
    if app in APPS:
        command = APPS[app][0]
        return "" if shutil.which(command[0]) else f"{command[0]} not installed"
    if app in ("launcher", "fcitx5-launcher") and not os.access(launcher, os.X_OK):
        return f"no {launcher} (cargo build --release in launcher/, or PILA_LAUNCHER_BIN)"
    if app == "bar" and not os.access(bar, os.X_OK):
        return f"no {bar} (cargo build --release in launcher/, or PILA_BAR_BIN)"
    if app == "switcher" and not os.access(switcher, os.X_OK):
        return f"no {switcher} (cargo build --release in launcher/, or PILA_SWITCHER_BIN)"
    if app == "osd" and not os.access(osd, os.X_OK):
        return f"no {osd} (cargo build --release in launcher/, or PILA_OSD_BIN)"
    if app in ("launcher", "bar", "switcher", "osd"):
        return "" if shutil.which("foot") else "foot not installed"
    command, how = IME_APPS[app]
    tools = ([command("")[0]] if command else []) + ["fcitx5"]
    tools += ["wl-paste"] if how in ("clipboard", "launcher") else []
    for tool in tools:
        if not shutil.which(tool):
            return f"{tool} not installed"
    if not data_file("fcitx5/addon/rime.conf") or not data_file("rime-data/luna_pinyin.schema.yaml"):
        return "fcitx5 has no Rime with luna_pinyin"
    return ""


def main(argv):
    if len(argv) >= 3 and argv[0] == "--workload":
        Workload(argv[1], argv[2]).run()
        return 0
    if argv and argv[0] in ("-h", "--help"):
        print(__doc__)
        return 0
    names = list(APPS) + ["launcher", "bar", "switcher", "osd"] + list(IME_APPS)
    unknown = [a for a in argv if a not in names]
    if unknown:
        print(f"unknown app {unknown[0]!r}: one of {', '.join(names)}", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    repo = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
    pila = os.environ.get("PILA_BIN") or os.path.join(repo, "target/release/pila")
    if not os.access(pila, os.X_OK):
        print(f"no {pila}: build it (cargo build --release) or set PILA_BIN", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2
    for tool in ("dbus-run-session",):
        if not shutil.which(tool):
            print(f"{tool} is missing (package dbus)", file=sys.stderr)
            return 2
    launcher = os.environ.get("PILA_LAUNCHER_BIN") or os.path.join(
        repo, "launcher/target/release", LAUNCHER)
    bar = os.environ.get("PILA_BAR_BIN") or os.path.join(repo, "launcher/target/release", BAR_APP)
    switcher = os.environ.get("PILA_SWITCHER_BIN") or os.path.join(
        repo, "launcher/target/release", SWITCHER_APP)
    osd = os.environ.get("PILA_OSD_BIN") or os.path.join(repo, "launcher/target/release", OSD_APP)
    ok = True
    for app in argv or names:
        missing = missing_for(app, launcher, bar, switcher, osd)
        if missing:
            print(f"\nSKIP  {app} ({missing})")
            continue
        print(f"\nRunning {app} on a headless Pila...")
        out = os.path.join(repo, "pila-apps", app)
        shutil.rmtree(out, ignore_errors=True)
        os.makedirs(out)
        sealed = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="pila-apps-")
        home, run = os.path.join(sealed, "home"), os.path.join(sealed, "run")
        os.makedirs(home)
        os.makedirs(run, mode=0o700)
        config = os.path.join(sealed, "config.toml")
        with open(config, "w") as f:
            f.write('# Written by scripts/apps.\nmod = "super"\n')
            if app in ("launcher", "fcitx5-launcher"):
                f.write(f'launcher = "{launcher} --terminal foot"\n')
        env = {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items()
               if k not in ("WAYLAND_DISPLAY", "DISPLAY", "DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS", "PILA_SOCKET",
                            "NIRI_SOCKET", "SWAYSOCK", "I3SOCK", "HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE",
                            "XDG_SESSION_DESKTOP", "DESKTOP_SESSION",
                            # Apps reach the input method through Pila.
                            "GTK_IM_MODULE", "QT_IM_MODULE", "XMODIFIERS")}
        env.update(HOME=home, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=run, XDG_CONFIG_HOME=os.path.join(home, ".config"),
                   XDG_STATE_HOME=os.path.join(home, ".local/state"),
                   XDG_CACHE_HOME=os.path.join(home, ".cache"),
                   XDG_DATA_HOME=os.path.join(home, ".local/share"),
                   PILA_HEADLESS_CHECK_INVARIANTS="1", PILA_APPS_BAR=os.path.abspath(bar),
                   PILA_APPS_SWITCHER=os.path.abspath(switcher),
                   PILA_APPS_OSD=os.path.abspath(osd),
                   RUST_LOG=env.get("PILA_APPS_RUST_LOG", "info,pila=debug,pila::frames=info"))
        workload = f"python3 -I {os.path.abspath(__file__)} --workload {app} {out}"
        with open(os.path.join(out, "pila.log"), "w") as log:
            try:
                subprocess.run(["timeout", "180", "dbus-run-session", "--", pila, "--backend", "headless",
                                "--headless-outputs", "eDP-1:1920x1080@60", "--config", config,
                                "-c", workload],
                               env=env, stdout=log, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, check=False)
            finally:
                shutil.rmtree(sealed, ignore_errors=True)
        ok = judge(app, out) and ok
    print()
    print("All checks passed." if ok else "Some checks failed: see pila-apps/<app>/pila.log and steps.")
    return 0 if ok else 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
